---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import DisplayTitle from '../components/DisplayTitle.astro'
import BenefitPicker from '../components/benefits/BenefitPicker.astro'
import BenefitSection from '../components/benefits/BenefitSection.astro'
import { benefitEntries, defaultEntrySlug } from '../components/benefits/entries'
---

<Layout title="What your country and your role gets" description="What citizens, workers, businesses and countries gain from EU digital and language reform, broken down by who you are.">
  <div class="container mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-8">
    <DisplayTitle title="What this gets your country, and you" />

    <div class="mb-4" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: var(--text-xl);">
      Every European country is aging, and each one hits the wall with a different economy,
      a different industry and a different set of neighbours. Pick yours, or pick the role
      you would play, and read the version of the argument that concerns you.
    </div>

    <p class="mb-10" style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
      Each answer follows the same three layers: a shared working language, a digital state
      built on top of it, and machines cheap enough to do the work there will not be enough
      people to do. Running through all of them: who ends up owning the gains.
      <a href="/why" class="underline underline-offset-4" style="color: var(--color-accent-primary);"
        >Read why Europe has to reform</a
      >.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 md:gap-8">
      <div class="w-full md:w-72 flex-shrink-0">
        <div class="md:sticky md:top-4">
          <BenefitPicker activeSlug={defaultEntrySlug} swapInPlace={true} />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="flex-grow">
        {
          benefitEntries.map((entry) => (
            <BenefitSection entry={entry} hidden={entry.slug !== defaultEntrySlug} />
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
